+The concurrency mechanism belongs to record-store, not this HLD. Record-store keeps every submitted visit intact as a whole-visit revision and holds competing revisions for coordinator review instead of combining them. Tablet-sync and review-export build on that node's contract: it fixes the submission metadata, the shape of review work, and which visits offer a current revision to an export. Both link to record-store rather than define their own concurrency semantics.
+
+## Vocabulary
+
+- **Revision**: one accepted submission of a complete visit, kept unchanged.
+- **Base revision**: the revision a worker's copy of a visit started from.
+- **Competing revisions**: revisions of one visit that a coordinator has not yet resolved into one.
+- **Unresolved visit**: a visit with competing revisions; it has no current revision.
 
